CREATED:20231004T171957Z
DESCRIPTION:Large language model pretraining is generally compute bound and
  rather expensive. Recent AI accelerators have started supporting (MX)FP4 G
 EMMs\, which can be 2X faster than FP8 GEMMs in hardware. In this work\, we
  introduce the first pretraining recipe that leverages MXFP4 GEMMs while in
 curring minimal degradation over BF16 mixed precision training. Our method 
 hinges on computing unbiased gradient estimates\, which enables more accura
 te updates in expectation. Specifically\, we modify the OCP quantization al
 gorithm to be unbiased and use a memory-bound construction of the random Ha
 damard transform to theoretically bound the variance of gradient estimates.
  Our recipe computes over half of the training FLOPs in MXFP4\, enabling an
  estimated E2E speedup of >1.3X over FP8 in the backward pass.\n\n-::~:~::~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~
