DESCRIPTION:We will explore quality-diversity optimization to improve fairn
 ess across skin tones in facial recognition systems by sampling diverse\, s
 ynthetic facial datasets from the generative StyleGAN2 model\n\nAllen's Bio
 : Allen Chang is an incoming PhD student at UPenn NLP\, where he will be ad
 vised by Prof. Mark Yatskar. Previously\, he completed his BS in Computer S
 cience at the University of Southern California (USC) working with Profs. M
 aja Matarić\, Jesse Thomason\, and Stefanos Nikolaidis. His current interes
 ts are language grounding\, social inference and reasoning\, and learning f
 rom synthetic data.\n\nThe associated paper for the session is @ https://ar
 xiv.org/abs/2312.14369 \n\n Allen's webpage is @ https://www.cylumn.com/\n\
 n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
