DESCRIPTION:The discussion will explore Common-Sense Bias Discovery (CSBD)\
 , a novel method leveraging image descriptions to identify and mitigate bia
 ses in image classification by adjusting sampling weights\, significantly o
 utperforming current bias mitigation techniques without needing sensitive l
 abels.<br><br>The associated paper for the session is @ <a href="https://ar
 xiv.org/abs/2401.13213"><u>https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.13213</u></a><br><br>
 Miao's Bio:  Miao is a a CS Ph.D. student at New York University (NYU) and 
 a Graduate Researcher at the The Visualization and Data Analytics Research 
 Center at NYU. (<a href="https://vida.engineering.nyu.edu/">https://vida.en
 gineering.nyu.edu/</a>) Her research direction lies at the intersection of 
 computer vision and fairness/bias mitigation\, applied on real-world enviro
 nmental and healthcare problems.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: ht
