DESCRIPTION:The discussion will explore training CLIP models with synthetic
  data\, focusing on the paper's methodologies\, their effectiveness versus 
 real data\, and future research and application impacts in AI and computer 
 vision.<br><br>The associated paper for the session is @ <a href="https://a
 rxiv.org/abs/2402.01832"><u>https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.01832</u></a><br><br
 >Fabio's Bio:  Fabio is a postdoctoral researcher in the Torr Vision Group 
 (<a href="https://torrvision.com/index.html">https://torrvision.com/index.h
 tml</a>) at the University of Oxford\, working with Phil Torr. Previously\,
  Fabio was a co-tutelle PhD at Vislab/Ambarella\, located in Parma (Italy) 
 and Inria Astra-vision team\, in Paris (France)\, where he was supervised b
 y Raoul de Charette. Fabio is currently working on large scale diffusion mo
 dels for image generation\, and continual learning.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:
