DESCRIPTION:Bio:  Mike is an astrophysicist at the University of Toronto. H
 e works on combining crowdsourcing and deep learning to measure the appeara
 nce of millions of galaxies\, helping to understand why galaxies look the w
 ay they do. His galaxy foundation models have been used on every major tele
 scope. He is interested in the "full stack" of practical problems with usin
 g models for science\, from model-in-the-loop annotation to quantifying pre
 diction biases.<br><br>The associated paper for the session is @ <a href="h
 ttps://arxiv.org/abs/2404.02973" target="_blank"><u>https://arxiv.org/abs/2
 404.02973</u></a>\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
