DESCRIPTION:"Shape-Image Correspondences with no Keypoint Supervision"<br><
 br>In this session\, we will explore SHIC: Unsupervised techniques for imag
 e-to-3D shape correspondences using advanced foundation models <br><br>Alek
 sandar is a final-year PhD student in the Visual Geometry Group at Oxford (
 <a href="https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/)\,">https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/
 ~vgg/)\,</a> supervised by Andrea Vedaldi and Christian Rupprecht. His PhD 
 focuses on unsupervised learning\, multi-modality\, and foundational models
 . He has also worked on evaluating LLMs for sciences and removing societal 
 biases from large models.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: https://m
 eet.google.com/dhk-skzx-uqi\nOr dial: (US) +1 562-419-2161 PIN: 511075208#\
 nMore phone numbers: https://tel.meet/dhk-skzx-uqi?pin=8749693677858&hs=7\n
 \nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/92827
 20\n\nPlease do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
