ORGANIZER;CN=c_4149d91b043a3a683b70c2b2b7697f98a8c57a6529c114eed60664456cea
 1fef@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:c_4149d91b043a3a683b70c2b2b7697f98a8c
 57a6529c114eed60664456cea1fef@group.calendar.google.com
UID:jvci69us7u30l7ef3qn2iak114_R20250128T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=DECLINED;CN=avinab
 neogy.bits@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:avinabneogy.bits@gmail.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/sqj-qimt-yno
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250128T080000
CREATED:20231004T175955Z
DESCRIPTION:<ol><u><a target="_blank" href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.1537
 0"></a></u></ol><span>Modern deep policy gradient methods achieve effective
  performance on simulated robotic tasks\, but they all require large replay
  buffers or expensive batch updates\, or both\, making them incompatible fo
 r real systems with resource-limited computers. First\, I will show that th
 ese methods fail catastrophically when limited to small replay buffers or d
 uring streaming/incremental learning\, where updates only use the most rece
 nt sample without batch updates or a replay buffer. Then\, I will introduce
  our novel incremental deep policy gradient method --- Action Value Gradien
 t (AVG) and a set of normalization and scaling techniques to address the ch
 allenges of instability in incremental learning. Finally\, I will present r
 esults showcasing effective deep reinforcement learning on both simulated b
 enchmarks and real robots using only incremental updates—marking a signific
 ant advancement in real-time reinforcement learning for practical applicati
 ons. Our NeurIPS paper: </span><u><a target="_blank" href="https://arxiv.or
 g/abs/2411.15370">https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.15370</a></u><br><br>Gautham V
 asan is a PhD student at the University of Alberta\, advised by Dr. Rupam M
 ahmood. He is interested in building machines with animal-like intelligence
 \, specifically robots that can continually learn\, adapt\, develop\, and i
 mprove throughout their lifetimes. His research focuses on policy gradient 
 methods\, real-time learning and continual learning systems. Previously\, h
 e was a Machine Learning Researcher at Kindred AI\, leveraging deep RL to i
 dentify apparel items to pick\, place and sort into complete end-customer o
 rders at e-commerce fulfilment centres for companies such as Gap and Americ
 an Eagle.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/s
 qj-qimt-yno\nOr dial: (US) +1 916-229-6615 PIN: 566139271#\nMore phone numb
 ers: https://tel.meet/sqj-qimt-yno?pin=1750950340211&hs=7\n\nLearn more abo
 ut Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nPlease do 
 not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
LAST-MODIFIED:20250615T231056Z
SEQUENCE:8
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:C4AI - Gautham Vasan - Streaming Deep Reinforcement Learning (RL) 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
