DESCRIPTION:Quantization is a powerful technique for accelerating large lan
 guage model (LLM) inference\, delivering significant gains in efficiency. Y
 et\, for newcomers\, the rapid evolution of methods and the complexity of t
 he field can feel overwhelming. This tutorial is designed to demystify quan
 tization and provide a solid foundation for beginners and practitioners ali
 ke.\nInstead of focusing on a single technique\, we take a first-principles
  approach to understanding quantization. We begin with an accessible introd
 uction to key concepts and the most widely used quantization formats. From 
 there\, we explore the why\, when\, and how of quantizing LLMs\, emphasizin
 g practical insights into the bottlenecks of the forward pass and how quant
 ization addresses them. Participants will learn how to optimize various sta
 ges of LLM inference while weighing the trade-offs between speed\, efficien
 cy\, and accuracy.\nThe hands-on portion of the tutorial guides attendees t
 hrough practical examples\, demonstrating how to apply and calibrate differ
 ent quantization methods on leading open-source LLMs. By the end\, particip
 ants will gain actionable knowledge on selecting the right quantization str
 ategies and fine-tuning them to achieve optimal accuracy-recovery results.\
 n\nEldar Kurtić is a Senior Researcher at Red Hat and Institute of Science 
 and Technology Austria\, specializing in efficient inference techniques for
  large language models (LLMs)\, with a particular focus on sparsity and qua
 ntization. His work centers on developing methods to accelerate inference w
 ithin the vLLM engine\, bridging cutting-edge research with practical deplo
 yment solutions. Outside of his primary research\, Eldar enjoys finding and
  fixing bugs in large-scale machine learning projects\, contributing to the
  robustness of open-source AI ecosystems.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google
  Meet: https://meet.google.com/nvg-ptgt-ucf\nOr dial: (US) +1 575-942-2037 
 PIN: 559285433#\nMore phone numbers: https://tel.meet/nvg-ptgt-ucf?pin=8389
 948644310&hs=7\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/us
 ers/answer/9282720\n\nPlease do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~
