DESCRIPTION:This talk presents two recent advances in making generative AI 
 systems more interactive and controllable. First\, I will introduce ReCaptu
 re\, a novel method that enables users to regenerate existing videos with n
 ew camera trajectories\, allowing for cinematic effects like pans\, tilts\,
  and orbital shots while maintaining scene dynamics. ReCapture achieves thi
 s through a two-stage approach combining multiview diffusion models with ma
 sked video fine-tuning. Second\, I will present Unbounded\, a novel "genera
 tive infinite game" that enables open-ended character life simulation throu
 gh the integration of specialized language models and dynamic visual genera
 tion. Unbounded features innovations in both LLM distillation for real-time
  game mechanics and a novel regional image prompt adapter for consistent ch
 aracter visualization. Together\, these works demonstrate how generative AI
  can enhance creative control and enable new forms of interactive digital e
 xperiences\, with potential extensions into virtual generative worlds\n\nNa
 taniel is a Senior Research Scientist at Google. He completed his PhD at Bo
 ston University\, advised by Professor Stan Sclaroff. He is mostly known fo
 r his work in personalization of image and video generation models and his 
 work as lead author of DreamBooth.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: 
