DESCRIPTION:This session is part of the <b>Cohere Labs Open Science Communi
 ty Summer School</b>\, a learning initiative featuring some of the leading 
 minds in machine learning from INRIA\, META (FAIR)\, Google DeepMind\, Cohe
 re Labs and more.<a href="https://sites.google.com/cohere.com/coherelabs-co
 mmunity/community-programs/summer-school" target="_blank"> Learn more about
  all upcoming speakers in this event series.</a><br><br><p dir="ltr">In thi
 s session\, we will explore the fundamentals of self-supervised learning (S
 SL) in computer vision\, a powerful approach that enables models to learn u
 seful image representations without labeled data. We’ll start with the core
  principles and motivations behind SSL\, introduce the main families of met
 hods such as contrastive learning and masked image modeling\, and progressi
 vely build toward understanding the architecture and training strategies of
  DINOv2\, a state-of-the-art SSL model for visual representation learning. 
 By the end\, you'll have a clear picture of how DINOv2 works and how it's u
 sed in real-world applications like image retrieval\, classification\, or s
 egmentation.</p>\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.googl
 e.com/gtf-rhad-dkc\nOr dial: (US) +1 530-500-4078 PIN: 403065957#\nMore pho
 ne numbers: https://tel.meet/gtf-rhad-dkc?pin=9878535963402&hs=7\n\nLearn m
 ore about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nPle
 ase do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
LAST-MODIFIED:20250620T161858Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Timothée Darcet - Scaling Self-Supervised Learning for Vision: An I
 ntroduction to DINOv2 (Summer School)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
