DESCRIPTION:This session is part of the <b>Cohere Labs Open Science Communi
 ty Summer School</b>\, a learning initiative featuring some of the leading 
 minds in machine learning from INRIA\, META (FAIR)\, Google DeepMind\, Cohe
 re Labs and more.<a href="https://sites.google.com/cohere.com/coherelabs-co
 mmunity/community-programs/summer-school" target="_blank"> Learn more about
  all upcoming speakers in this event series.</a><br><br><p dir="ltr">This s
 ession will explore Diffusion Models. We'll start with the fundamentals of 
 foundational Denoising Diffusion Probabilistic Models (DDPMs) and their mor
 e efficient\, deterministic successors\, Denoising Diffusion Implicit Model
 s (DDIMs). The discussion will also address the critical function of noise 
 schedules in controlling the generation process. Finally\, we will introduc
 e flow matching\, a modern framework that offers a more direct approach to 
 transforming a simple distribution into complex data</p>\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJ
 oin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/gtf-rhad-dkc\nOr dial: (US) +
 1 530-500-4078 PIN: 403065957#\nMore phone numbers: https://tel.meet/gtf-rh
 ad-dkc?pin=9878535963402&hs=7\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.
 google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nPlease do not edit this section.\n-::~
 :~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 ::~:~::-
