ORGANIZER;CN=c_4149d91b043a3a683b70c2b2b7697f98a8c57a6529c114eed60664456cea
 1fef@group.calendar.google.com:mailto:c_4149d91b043a3a683b70c2b2b7697f98a8c
 57a6529c114eed60664456cea1fef@group.calendar.google.com
UID:3bea6banij6spmsnbmghe2e39n_R20250706T160000@google.com
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=NEEDS-ACTION;CN=av
 inabneogy.bits@gmail.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=0:mailto:avinabneogy.bits@gmail.com
X-GOOGLE-CONFERENCE:https://meet.google.com/gtf-rhad-dkc
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20250709T090000
CREATED:20250619T161846Z
DESCRIPTION:This session is part of the <b>Cohere Labs Open Science Communi
 ty Summer School</b>\, a learning initiative featuring some of the leading 
 minds in machine learning from INRIA\, META (FAIR)\, Google DeepMind\, Cohe
 re Labs and more.<a href="https://sites.google.com/cohere.com/coherelabs-co
 mmunity/community-programs/summer-school" target="_blank"> Learn more about
  all upcoming speakers in this event series.</a><br><br><p dir="ltr">This s
 ession explores how transformer-based language models make predictions by e
 xamining their relationship to simple N-gram statistical rules derived from
  training data. We'll discuss novel findings including: (1) an approximatio
 n criterion showing that low-variance predictions tend to be well-described
  by N-gram rules\, (2) how transformers exhibit curriculum learning dynamic
 s by progressing from simple to complex statistical patterns\, and (3) a tr
 aining-intrinsic method for detecting overfitting without holdout data. The
  work demonstrates that up to 79% of transformer predictions on TinyStories
  can be matched by optimal N-gram rules\, providing quantitative insights i
 nto the statistical structure underlying LLM behavior. We'll also examine t
 he implications for understanding memorization\, generalization\, and the b
 rittleness of language models.</p>\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: 
 https://meet.google.com/gtf-rhad-dkc\nOr dial: (US) +1 530-500-4078 PIN: 40
 3065957#\nMore phone numbers: https://tel.meet/gtf-rhad-dkc?pin=98785359634
 02&hs=7\n\nLearn more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/ans
 wer/9282720\n\nPlease do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
LAST-MODIFIED:20250620T161858Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Timothee Nguyen - Understanding Transformers via N-gram Statistics 
 (Summer School)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
