CREATED:20250619T161846Z
DESCRIPTION:This session is part of the <b>Cohere Labs Open Science Communi
 ty Summer School</b>\, a learning initiative featuring some of the leading 
 minds in machine learning from INRIA\, META (FAIR)\, Google DeepMind\, Cohe
 re Labs and more.<a href="https://sites.google.com/cohere.com/coherelabs-co
 mmunity/community-programs/summer-school" target="_blank"> Learn more about
  all upcoming speakers in this event series.</a><br><br><p dir="ltr">As LLM
 s hit diminishing returns from traditional growth\, test-time inference off
 ers a promising path forward. I’ll present a particle-based scaling method 
 that avoids the early pruning pitfalls of deterministic search by maintaini
 ng diverse candidates and balancing exploration with exploitation. This sim
 ple yet efficient approach enables small 1.5B models to outperform GPT-4o i
 n just 4 rollouts and scales 7B models to o1 performance in 32.</p>\n\n-::~
 :~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 ::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.google.com/gtf-rhad-dkc\nOr d
