DESCRIPTION:This session we will look into the innovative integration of La
 rge Language Models (LLMs) within MARMAR's medication management platform t
 o enhance drug form classification. By harnessing the power of a generative
  model and a Medical BERT model\, the result is a robust dataset of +3k med
 ications and their respective forms.\n\nAhmad Rufai Yusuf is a designer\, A
 I research engineer\, and the founder of MARMAR\, an AI-powered medication 
 safety platform designed to personalize drug interaction analysis and mitig
 ate the risks of inappropriate polypharmacy. He holds a background in Artif
 icial Intelligence and Sustainable Technologies from Tomorrow University of
  Applied Sciences. His work focuses on LLMs\, NLP for healthcare\, NLP for 
 African languages\, and AI safety—particularly in clinical applications.\n\
