DESCRIPTION:Through this session\, Evelyn will lead an insightful discussio
 n on understanding and addressing the low adoption rates of AI tools among 
 women.\n\nSpeaker bio:\nAsio Evelyn Patra is a UX Designer\, Data Analyst\,
  and Research Fellow at the Uganda National Institute of Public Health\, fo
 cusing on digitizing birth registration systems under the BIS project. She 
 also lectures at Makerere University’s School of Computing and Informatics 
 Technology and facilitates graduate-level courses in Health Informatics at 
 both MakSPH and UNIPH. Evelyn specializes in designing intelligent user int
 erfaces and digital platforms for health\, e-government\, and e-commerce\, 
 with expertise in data analytics\, remote monitoring\, and sensor-based sys
 tems. Her research intersects health informatics\, AI\, and service design\
 , addressing challenges in disaster response\, mental health\, aging\, and 
 governance. She actively mentors undergraduate students in tech innovation\
 , while contributing to the Development Informatics research group. Passion
 ate about user-centered and data-driven design\, Evelyn is committed to lev
 eraging emerging technologies for public good and driving innovation in Uga
 nda’s digital transformation landscape.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
