CREATED:20231004T173832Z
DESCRIPTION:When leveraging language models for reasoning tasks\, generatin
 g explicit chain-of-thought (CoT) steps are often crucial for high accuracy
 . In this work\, drawing inspiration from how the human brain transitions f
 rom explicit\, conscious\, deliberate reasoning (System 2) to implicit\, au
 tomatic\, intuitive thinking (System 1)\, we seek to internalize explicit C
 oT reasoning within a model that directly produces the final answer\, which
  we define as the implicit CoT paradigm.<br><br>To realize implicit CoT\, w
 e found a simple yet effective method: starting with a model trained for ex
 plicit CoT reasoning\, we gradually remove the intermediate steps and finet
 une the model. This approach enables a finetuned GPT-2 Small model to solve
  20-by-20 multiplication with up to 99.5% accuracy\, whereas standard train
 ing cannot solve beyond 4-by-4 multiplication.<br><br>You can try our demo 
 at <a href="https://huggingface.co/spaces/yuntian-deng/gpt2-multiplication"
 >https://huggingface.co/spaces/yuntian-deng/gpt2-multiplication</a><br><br>
 Yuntian Deng is an assistant professor at the University of Waterloo and a 
 visiting professor at NVIDIA mentored by Prof. Yejin Choi. He was previousl
 y a postdoc at AI2\, also advised by Prof. Choi. He received his PhD from H
 arvard University under the supervision of Prof. Alexander Rush and Prof. S
 tuart Shieber. His research focuses on natural language processing and mach
 ine learning. His recent works include WildChat and implicit chain-of-thoug
 ht reasoning. He is a key contributor to OpenNMT\, steganography.live\, ope
 naiwatch.com\, latex-to-image\, and image-to-latex. He is the recipient of 
 an Nvidia Fellowship\, a Baidu Fellowship\, a University of Chicago Rising 
 Stars in Data Science\, an ACM Gordon Bell Prize\, and an ACL best demo awa
 rd runner up. You can learn more about him at yuntiandeng.com.\n\n-::~:~::~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~
