DESCRIPTION:Join Mila's Michael Noukhovitch to discuss a critical bottlenec
 k in LLM development: the computational cost of on-policy RLHF. He will pre
 sent his work on Asynchronous RLHF\, a paradigm that decouples data generat
 ion and training to unlock massive compute efficiency. This is a must-see f
 or researchers interested in practical methods for scaling models\, demonst
 rating up to a 70% training speedup without a performance trade-off. The ta
 lk provides a powerful case study on bridging SOTA engineering with researc
 h to create more robust and scalable training methods\, so bring your quest
 ions for the live Q&A!\n\nMichael Noukhovitch is a final year PhD student w
 ith Aaron Courville at Mila\, University of Montreal working at the interse
 ction of language and reinforcement learning. Generally\, he has published 
 on RLHF: increasing robustness\, training efficiently\, and reducing alignm
 ent tax. Pre-LLMs\, he was working on learning communication in multi-agent
  RL\, co-organizing the NeurIPS/ICLR EmeCom workshops. He is currently inte
 rning at Allen AI working on post-training the next generation of open-sour
 ce LLMs. Previously\, has also done research as an intern at Google and Met
 a\, a visiting researcher at ServiceNow\, and consulted on AI art for Centr
 e PHI in Montreal.\n\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~
 :~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-\nJoin with Google Meet: https://meet.goo
 gle.com/bbq-ipwu-anj\nOr dial: (US) +1 929-399-6751 PIN: 388079609#\nMore p
 hone numbers: https://tel.meet/bbq-ipwu-anj?pin=6478779386607&hs=7\n\nLearn
  more about Meet at: https://support.google.com/a/users/answer/9282720\n\nP
 lease do not edit this section.\n-::~:~::~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:
 ~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~:~::~:~::-
